<h2 style="color:#0f2744; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:20px; margin-bottom:8px; border-bottom:1.5px solid #0f2744; padding-bottom:4px;">ABSTRACT</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">In higher educational institutions, alumni constitute one of the most valuable resources for career mentorship, industry exposure, and campus placement support. However, conventional campus communication mechanisms—such as fragmented WhatsApp groups, disparate social media pages, and periodic alumni meets—lack structured categorization, cross-batch searchability, and institutional coordination. Current students frequently struggle to identify seniors working in targeted industries, and alumni lack a streamlined institutional portal to post verified internships and career advice.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;"><strong>JIMS Alumni Network</strong> is a full-stack, responsive web application and digital campus portal designed to bridge the gap between current students, alumni, and official placement bodies of Jagan Institute of Management Studies. The application is designed as a modern decoupled client-server architecture:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Frontend Presentation Layer</strong>: Developed using <strong>React 19</strong> and bundled with <strong>Vite</strong>, featuring a responsive desktop and mobile interface, multi-category feed filtering, real-time directory search, optimistic UI toggles, and dynamic campus metrics.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Backend API Layer</strong>: Built on <strong>Node.js</strong> and <strong>Express.js</strong>, providing secure RESTful API endpoints for authentication, community discussion posts, directory queries, and campus internship listings.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Data & Persistence Layer</strong>: Powered by <strong>MongoDB</strong> with <strong>Mongoose ODM</strong> schemas, supplemented by a <strong>Resilient Dual-Mode Architecture</strong> featuring automatic fallback to an in-memory interactive dataset. This design ensures 100% demonstration uptime regardless of local database availability.</li>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The portal provides core modules including <strong>Role-Based Authentication (Student, Alumni, Official)</strong>, <strong>Community Feed & Discussions</strong>, <strong>Student & Alumni Directory</strong>, <strong>Campus Internship & Career Board</strong>, and <strong>Profile & Academic Credential Verification</strong>. This report presents the requirement analysis, system architecture, data models, procedural workflows, test cases, and evaluation results for the Phase 1 release of the system.</p>
<div style="page-break-before:always; border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1; margin:20px 0;"></div>
