<h1 style="color:#0f2744; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:22pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:24px; margin-bottom:10px; text-align:center;">CHAPTER 1: INTRODUCTION</h1>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">1.1 Background</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">Higher educational institutions cultivate extensive alumni networks comprising professionals, entrepreneurs, researchers, and corporate executives. These individuals possess real-world industry experience and technical insights that are invaluable for current students undergoing academic preparation. </p>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">At Jagan Institute of Management Studies (JIMS), students across disciplines—including BCA, MCA, BBA, and B.Tech—require guidance regarding technical interview rounds, full-stack development practices, competitive programming, and placement drives. Traditionally, interaction with alumni occurs through informal social media channels, unindexed messaging groups, or infrequent annual alumni meets. These methods suffer from lack of verification, inability to filter seniors by technical skills or industry domain, and lack of continuity. </p>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">Furthermore, faculty and the Training and Placement Cell require a centralized platform to announce placement workshops, invite alumni for mock technical interviews, and publish verified internship opportunities. <strong>JIMS Alumni Network</strong> addresses these challenges by delivering an institution-centric web portal tailored specifically to the JIMS campus community.</p>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">1.2 Objectives</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The primary objectives of the JIMS Alumni Network project are:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Centralized Campus Connectivity</strong>: Provide a unified digital portal connecting students, alumni mentors, and institutional placement bodies.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Searchable Member Directory</strong>: Deliver a high-speed search and filtering engine allowing students to find seniors by name, batch, department, technical competencies, and company.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Interactive Knowledge Sharing</strong>: Establish a campus feed where alumni share technical interview advice and faculty announce placement workshops, complete with category tags and discussion threads.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Curated Internship Board</strong>: Create a job board displaying campus internships with company name, location (Remote / On-Site), stipend, required competencies, application deadlines, and one-click application tracking.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Architectural Reliability (Zero-Fail Showcase)</strong>: Build a resilient client-server architecture with an integrated API health adapter and automated fallback mechanism to guarantee uninterrupted operation during evaluation.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">1.3 Purpose, Scope, and Applicability</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">1.3.1 Purpose</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The purpose of the system is to establish a dedicated, secure, and structured medium for professional networking within JIMS Rohini. It democratizes access to alumni mentorship, empowers students to seek career advice, and offers alumni a structured platform to contribute to their alma mater.</p>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">1.3.2 Scope</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The scope of Phase 1 includes:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Role-based profile management covering Students, Alumni, and Official Campus Representatives.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Real-time Community Feed with optimistic like toggling and threaded comments.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Searchable Directory with dual-mode views (Sidebar suggestions & Full Directory) and connection state management.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Dedicated Campus Internships board with remote/on-site filtering and application state toggling.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">RESTful API backend built on Express and Node.js with MongoDB data schemas.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Dual-mode client integration providing live MongoDB connectivity and in-memory prototype fallback.</li>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;"><em>Scope Exclusions (Reserved for Phase 2)</em>: Real-time WebSockets chat, third-party payment gateways, and automated LinkedIn OAuth integration.</p>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">1.3.3 Applicability</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The portal is directly applicable to:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Academic Departments</strong>: Organising guest lectures and departmental seminars.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Training and Placement Cell (T&P)</strong>: Disseminating workshop schedules, placement notifications, and hiring drives.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Current Students</strong>: Seeking project guidance, technical review, and internship opportunities.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Alumni Community</strong>: Networking with fellow graduates and recruiting junior talent.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">1.4 Achievements</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Implemented a clean, modern Single Page Application (SPA) using React 19 and Vite with fast sub-300ms production builds.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Developed an Express.js REST API with structured controllers, routes, and Mongoose schemas for Users, Posts, and Internships.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Established a zero-failure resilient API adapter in <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">src/services/api.js</code> that auto-detects API health and falls back to an interactive prototype store if the database is offline.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Designed a responsive user interface with navy blue (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">#0f2744</code>) and emerald theme colors, custom SVG iconography, and responsive grid layouts.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">1.5 Organisation of the Report</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">This report is organized into seven sequential chapters:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Chapter 1</strong> presents the project background, objectives, and scope.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Chapter 2</strong> surveys the technology stack and tooling choices.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Chapter 3</strong> analyzes functional requirements, feasibility, and DFD/ER conceptual models.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Chapter 4</strong> outlines system design, data schemas, algorithmic logic, and test cases.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Chapter 5</strong> details implementation approaches and core code modules.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Chapter 6</strong> discusses test execution results and user operating instructions.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Chapter 7</strong> concludes with limitations and future development scope.</li>
<div style="page-break-before:always; border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1; margin:20px 0;"></div>
<h1 style="color:#0f2744; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:22pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:24px; margin-bottom:10px; text-align:center;">CHAPTER 2: SURVEY OF TECHNOLOGIES</h1>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">2.1 Frontend Technologies</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2.1.1 React.js (Version 19)</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">React.js is a component-based open-source JavaScript library developed by Meta Platforms. React employs a Virtual DOM tree that compares current and subsequent UI states using a reconciliation algorithm. When state updates occur (such as toggling an internship application or filtering directory records), only the mutated DOM nodes are re-rendered. In this project, React 19 provides functional components, custom hooks, and state management via <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">useState</code> and <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">useEffect</code>.</p>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2.1.2 Vite (Version 8)</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">Vite is a modern build tool that leverages native browser ES Modules (ESM) during local development and uses Rollup for highly optimized production bundling. Vite provides Hot Module Replacement (HMR) within milliseconds, avoiding the overhead of legacy bundlers.</p>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2.1.3 Custom Modern CSS Architecture</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">A dedicated, vanilla CSS architecture was chosen for the presentation layer (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">src/App.css</code>). Utilizing CSS custom variables, CSS Grid, and Flexbox, the UI achieves a clean desktop sidebar-main layout, interactive cards, and full mobile responsiveness without heavy external utility overhead.</p>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">2.2 Backend Technologies</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2.2.1 Node.js (Version 20+)</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">Node.js is an open-source, cross-platform runtime environment built on Google Chrome's V8 JavaScript engine. Node.js utilizes an asynchronous, event-driven, non-blocking I/O model based on an Event Loop, making it suitable for scalable network applications and RESTful microservices.</p>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2.2.2 Express.js (Version 5)</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">Express is a minimal and flexible web application framework for Node.js. It provides a robust suite of features for routing, HTTP request handling, middleware pipelines, and JSON payload serialization.</p>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2.2.3 Authentication & Security Libraries</h4>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>jsonwebtoken (JWT)</strong>: Used for stateless token-based authorization.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>bcryptjs</strong>: Implements an adaptive one-way hashing function with configurable salt rounds (10 rounds) to securely hash passwords before persistence.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>cors</strong>: Configured as middleware to govern cross-origin HTTP requests between the Vite development server (port 5173) and the Express API (port 5000).</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">2.3 Database Technologies</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2.3.1 MongoDB</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">MongoDB is a document-oriented, NoSQL database designed for high availability, horizontal scaling, and flexible document modeling. Data is stored in binary JSON format (BSON), enabling nested data structures such as skill arrays, tag lists, and applicant references without requiring multi-table SQL join operations.</p>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2.3.2 Mongoose ODM (Version 9)</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">Mongoose provides an Object Data Modeling (ODM) layer for MongoDB in Node.js. It manages schema definitions, data type casting, validation rules, default constraints, query building, and document middleware.</p>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">Table No. 2.01: Summary of Technology Stack</h3>
