<h1 style="color:#0f2744; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:22pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:24px; margin-bottom:10px; text-align:center;">CHAPTER 3: REQUIREMENTS AND ANALYSIS</h1>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">3.1 Problem Definition & Proposed System</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">3.1.1 Problem Definition</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The absence of an institution-specific alumni portal leads to several persistent operational bottlenecks:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Scattered Information</strong>: Alumni contact details are distributed across obsolete spreadsheets and personal address books.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Mentorship Hesitation</strong>: Students lack confidence contacting seniors on general platforms like LinkedIn due to unverified alumni status and uncertainty regarding mentorship willingness.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Ineffective Placement Outreach</strong>: Faculty coordinators spend significant manual effort contacting alumni individually for campus interview guidance.</li>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">3.1.2 Proposed System</h4>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The proposed <strong>JIMS Alumni Network</strong> provides an authenticated, searchable, and structured environment:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Real-time directory indexed by skills, batch, and current company.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Campus discussion feed organized by academic and placement categories.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Verified internship notices posted with stipend, skills, and application deadlines.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Interactive feedback loops with instantaneous state feedback.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">3.2 Feasibility Study</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Technical Feasibility</strong>: The chosen MERN stack components (Node.js, Express, React, MongoDB) are standard, mature, and actively maintained. The application runs efficiently on standard hardware.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Economic Feasibility</strong>: The entire system is built utilizing free, open-source software and developer tooling. No commercial licensing is required.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Operational Feasibility</strong>: The interface adopts familiar user experience patterns (feeds, cards, search filters, and badges), requiring zero specialized user training.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">3.3 Requirements Specification</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">3.3.1 Functional Requirements</h4>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">Table No. 3.01: Functional Requirements</h3>
