<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">4.4 Procedural Design & Core Algorithms</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">Algorithm 1: Like Toggle with Optimistic Feedback</h4>
<pre style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:12px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; white-space:pre-wrap; border-radius:4px;">Input: postId, currentUserId
1. Locate post by postId in database.
2. Check if currentUserId exists in post.likes array.
3. If exists:
      Remove currentUserId from post.likes (Unlike).
   Else:
      Append currentUserId to post.likes (Like).
4. Update post.likesCount = length(post.likes).
5. Save document and return updated count and boolean status.
</pre>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">Algorithm 2: Resilient Client-Server Synchronization</h4>
<pre style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:12px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; white-space:pre-wrap; border-radius:4px;">Input: API Health Probe Request
1. Execute fetch('/api/health') with 2000ms timeout.
2. If response received and status == 'online':
      Set apiStatus = 'online'.
      Fetch live posts, users, internships in parallel via Promise.all().
      Populate React state with database records.
3. Else:
      Catch network exception.
      Set apiStatus = 'prototype'.
      Populate React state from local initial mock store.
4. Render UI seamlessly without throwing blocking exceptions.
</pre>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">4.5 User Interface Design</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The user interface is centered around an institutional design system:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Color Palette</strong>: Midnight Blue (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">#0f2744</code>) for navigation and authority; Vibrant Emerald (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">#10b981</code>) for active statuses; Clean Slate (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">#f8fafc</code>) for readable card backgrounds.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Layout Structure</strong>: Fixed left sidebar for navigation across <em>Dashboard</em>, <em>Community Feed</em>, <em>Directory</em>, <em>Jobs & Internships</em>, and <em>My Profile</em>; dynamic top search bar; central card feed; right-hand widget sidebar displaying featured internships and suggested peers.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">4.6 Security Architecture</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Password Encryption</strong>: Passwords are encrypted using <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">bcryptjs</code> with salt round cost factor 10.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Protected Routes</strong>: Middleware verifies authentication tokens before allowing write operations.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Input Sanitization</strong>: API inputs are validated and trimmed to prevent script injection.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">4.7 Test Cases Design</h3>
