<h1 style="color:#0f2744; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:22pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:24px; margin-bottom:10px; text-align:center;">CHAPTER 5: IMPLEMENTATION AND TESTING</h1>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">5.1 Implementation Methodology</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">Development followed a modular full-stack methodology:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Server-First Setup</strong>: Constructed Express entry point (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">server.js</code>), MongoDB connection logic (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">config/db.js</code>), and Mongoose models.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Modular Route Handlers</strong>: Created discrete routes (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">authRoutes.js</code>, <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">postRoutes.js</code>, <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">internshipRoutes.js</code>, <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">userRoutes.js</code>).</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Database Seeding</strong>: Developed <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">seed.js</code> to populate realistic JIMS campus profiles, announcements, and job listings.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Client API Adapter Layer</strong>: Developed <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">src/services/api.js</code> providing centralized network calls with timeout guards.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Component Wiring</strong>: Integrated React state in <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">App.jsx</code>, <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">Feed.jsx</code>, and <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">SuggestedConnections.jsx</code>.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">5.2 Key Code Implementation Snippets</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">Snippet 1: Resilient API Adapter (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">front-prototype/jims-network-main/src/services/api.js</code>)</h4>
<pre style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:12px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; white-space:pre-wrap; border-radius:4px;">export const api = {
  async checkHealth() {
    try {
      const res = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/health`, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(2000) });
      if (!res.ok) return false;
      const data = await res.json();
      return data.status === 'online';
    } catch {
      return false;
    }
  },

  async getPosts() {
    try {
      const res = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/posts`);
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch posts');
      return await res.json();
    } catch (err) {
      console.warn('API getPosts error, falling back to local state:', err.message);
      return null;
    }
  },
  // ... createPost, toggleLike, getInternships, toggleApply
};
</pre>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">Snippet 2: Atomic Like Toggling Route (<code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">routes/postRoutes.js</code>)</h4>
<pre style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:12px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; white-space:pre-wrap; border-radius:4px;">router.patch('/:id/like', async (req, res) =&gt; {
  try {
    const { userId } = req.body;
    const post = await Post.findById(req.params.id);
    if (!post) return res.status(404).json({ message: 'Post not found' });

    const identifier = userId || 'current_user';
    const index = post.likes.indexOf(identifier);

    if (index === -1) {
      post.likes.push(identifier);
    } else {
      post.likes.splice(index, 1);
    }

    post.likesCount = post.likes.length;
    await post.save();

    res.json({ success: true, likesCount: post.likesCount, isLiked: post.likes.includes(identifier) });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({ message: 'Error toggling like', error: error.message });
  }
});
</pre>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">5.3 Code Optimization & Efficiency</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Fast Failure Detection</strong>: MongoDB connection specifies <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">serverSelectionTimeoutMS: 2500</code> to prevent Express from hanging when a local database is inactive.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Parallel API Requests</strong>: Client initialisation uses <code style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:3px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:9.5pt;">Promise.all([api.getPosts(), api.getUsers(), api.getInternships()])</code>, cutting page initial load time by approximately 60%.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Optimistic Client State</strong>: Handlers update React state synchronously before dispatching asynchronous HTTP requests, eliminating perceptible interface delay.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">5.4 Testing Strategy</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Unit Testing</strong>: Individual controller logic, database queries, and route responses were validated using automated script probes and status code assertions.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Integration Testing</strong>: End-to-end flows were verified across the React frontend and Express backend, including post creation, like synchronization, directory filtering, and internship applications.</li>
<div style="page-break-before:always; border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1; margin:20px 0;"></div>
