<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">6.2 User Documentation & Running the System</h3>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">1. Running the Backend Server</h4>
<pre style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:12px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; white-space:pre-wrap; border-radius:4px;"># Open terminal in project root:
npm start
# Server listens at http://localhost:5000
# Database seeding (optional): npm run seed
</pre>
<h4 style="color:#334155; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11.5pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:4px;">2. Running the Frontend Application</h4>
<pre style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:12px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; white-space:pre-wrap; border-radius:4px;"># In project root or frontend folder:
npm run dev
# OR: npm.cmd run dev
# Application opens at http://localhost:5173
</pre>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">6.3 Verification of Functional Deliverables</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">All core functional objectives outlined in Chapter 1 have been successfully verified:</p>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Verified real-time search across the student and alumni directory.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Verified category-tagged discussions with working like counters and comments.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Verified campus internships with Remote/On-Site filtering and application toggling.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;">Verified status badges indicating REST API connection versus prototype fallback mode.</li>
<div style="page-break-before:always; border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1; margin:20px 0;"></div>
<h1 style="color:#0f2744; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:22pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:24px; margin-bottom:10px; text-align:center;">CHAPTER 7: CONCLUSIONS AND FUTURE SCOPE</h1>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">7.1 Conclusion</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The <strong>JIMS Alumni Network</strong> successfully demonstrates a functional, full-stack campus networking portal tailored to the institutional requirements of JIMS Rohini. By pairing a responsive React 19 Single Page Application with an Express.js REST API and MongoDB data models, the system bridges the gap between current students, alumni mentors, and institutional placement bodies.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:10px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt; text-align:justify;">The implementation of a dual-mode resilient architecture ensures that the system delivers continuous, interactive demonstrations regardless of local database availability. The codebase follows modern software engineering principles, modular separation of concerns, and clean styling conventions.</p>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">7.2 System Limitations</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Real-Time Communication</strong>: Chat and immediate notification updates rely on HTTP polling rather than bi-directional WebSockets.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>File Uploads</strong>: Resumes and profile pictures currently utilize placeholder initials and document links rather than cloud object storage (e.g., AWS S3).</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Third-Party Integration</strong>: LinkedIn profiles are entered as verified URLs rather than through automated OAuth data synchronization.</li>
<h3 style="color:#1e3a8a; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:13pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:6px;">7.3 Future Enhancements</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Socket.io Integration</strong>: Implementation of bidirectional WebSocket channels for real-time one-to-one mentorship messaging and instant alerts.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Cloud Storage</strong>: Integration with AWS S3 or Cloudinary for direct PDF resume and profile photo uploads.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Alumni Verification Workflow</strong>: An administrative portal for college coordinators to verify alumni graduation credentials before issuing verified alumni badges.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Mobile Application</strong>: Porting the frontend architecture to React Native for native iOS and Android deployment.</li>
<div style="page-break-before:always; border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1; margin:20px 0;"></div>
