<h1 style="color:#0f2744; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:22pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:24px; margin-bottom:10px; text-align:center;">GLOSSARY</h1>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>API (Application Programming Interface)</strong>: A set of defined HTTP endpoints enabling communication between client applications and server services.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>BSON (Binary JSON)</strong>: A binary-encoded serialization format used by MongoDB for document storage.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)</strong>: A browser security mechanism governing cross-domain HTTP requests.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>HMR (Hot Module Replacement)</strong>: A build mechanism that exchanges, adds, or removes code modules in a running application without a full page reload.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>JWT (JSON Web Token)</strong>: An open standard (RFC 7519) compact, URL-safe means of securely transmitting claims between parties.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>ODM (Object Data Modeling)</strong>: An abstraction layer that manages data schema relationships between an object-oriented codebase and a document database.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>Optimistic UI</strong>: A frontend architectural pattern where the interface reflects state updates immediately, before server confirmation.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4px; line-height:1.5; font-size:11pt;"><strong>SPA (Single Page Application)</strong>: A web application that interacts with the browser by dynamically rewriting the current web page rather than loading complete new pages.</li>
<div style="page-break-before:always; border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1; margin:20px 0;"></div>
